ate of the underlying viewerThis is the only proc that tests the state of data.bufferIsConsistent-- RefText.AppendRope[to: data.buffer, from: r, start: loc.where + 1];Assumes data.buffer is consistentWhat if node goes away?What if node goes away?Assumes data.buffer is consistenterases last character, if any, in buffererases last "word" (consecutive run of letters and numbers), if any, in buffererases buffer back to (not including) previous CR, if anyGetCurrentBuffer[data];looks wrong ... why can't you backup past ready chars?Can't change echo stream, because "truth" about buffered characters is stored in Tioga document behind echo stream.Message Window Stream Module Initialization␀ÊA␀␀–"Cedar" style˜␀codešœ™Kšœ
